                    {
                        "sense_id": "abfce021-1d1f-354e-b642-5934ce697459",
                        "entry_id": "ade7b7af-b44e-334b-8c2d-bccf8de62fb4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A catarrh."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a4bba9ce-0aaf-4213-b6ab-f75046ac3d6f",
                                "sense_id": "abfce021-1d1f-354e-b642-5934ce697459",
                                "text": "The woodhacke, that syngeth ‘chur’,\nHorsly, as he had the mur; […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c6e26856-4fbd-45ba-802a-643a9ef2d3c8",
                                "sense_id": "abfce021-1d1f-354e-b642-5934ce697459",
                                "text": "[...] I like not his countenance; I am afraid he labours of the venereall murre."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6d1e1839-8dbd-41ae-b48b-84584da75b91",
                                "sense_id": "abfce021-1d1f-354e-b642-5934ce697459",
                                "text": "With them a Phthysique or consumption of the lungs is but an ordinary cough: A dysentery or bloody flux but a distemper of the stomacke; A pleurisie but a cold or murre; and as they gently name them so they easily endure them."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
